{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Welcome, I'm Dr. Aleman. Since you're new with us, let's confirm your full name and date of birth.",
   "start": 0.05,
   "end": 6.85
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Svetlana Petrovah. December 4th, 1979.",
   "start": 7.47,
   "end": 10.93
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And your new address?",
   "start": 11.79,
   "end": 12.91
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "4417 Juniper Ridge Drive. We moved here from Pittsburgh in August.",
   "start": 15.07,
   "end": 19.17
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "How's the move going?",
   "start": 19.95,
   "end": 21.27
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Boxes everywhere still. But the weather is much nicer. I won't miss the snow.",
   "start": 22.17,
   "end": 26.45
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'll bet, so I have the records your old doctor, Dr. Ostrowski, sent over. Tell me about your thyroid.",
   "start": 26.45,
   "end": 33.85
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I was diagnosed with Hashimoto's in 2015. I take Levothyric Sign, 88 micrograms every morning.",
   "start": 34.67,
   "end": 41.91
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "How do you take it? With food, coffee.",
   "start": 42.69,
   "end": 44.93
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Um, honestly, with my coffee and my calcium, all together. It's the only way I remember.",
   "start": 45.73,
   "end": 50.97
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, that's really common, and it's important. I'll come back to that. How have you been feeling?",
   "start": 51.59,
   "end": 57.29
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "A little more tired than usual, and I'm always cold. But I've also been moving furniture for two months, so who knows?",
   "start": 58.25,
   "end": 64.61
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any constipation, hair thinning, or weight changes?",
   "start": 65.23,
   "end": 68.29
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, my weight is the same. Hair's fine.",
   "start": 69.19,
   "end": 71.35
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any racing heart or palpitations?",
   "start": 72.01,
   "end": 74.41
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No.",
   "start": 75.36,
   "end": 75.82
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Your last TSH in the records from May was 5 .8, which is a bit high. And your cholesterol panel from May shows total cholesterol 248, LDL 164, HDL 52, and triglycerides 160.",
   "start": 75.82,
   "end": 92.86
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Dr. Ostrowski said to work on diet. I'm not on anything for it.",
   "start": 94.04,
   "end": 98.0
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any heart disease in the family.",
   "start": 98.42,
   "end": 100.52
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "My father had a heart attack at 58.",
   "start": 101.52,
   "end": 103.26
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "He's stents any other supplements besides the calcium",
   "start": 104.58,
   "end": 109.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "vitamin d 2000 units a day and a hair skin and nails gummy I think it has biotin the calcium is 600 milligrams once a day do you smoke never any allergies to medicines codine makes me throw up really badly got it",
   "start": 109.18,
   "end": 129.37
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "your Your blood pressure is 124 over 78, pulse 66, weight 158 pounds. Let me feel your neck. Thyroid isn't enlarged and I don't feel any nodules. Skin is a little dry, heart is regular, lungs are clear, and your reflexes are normal.",
   "start": 129.37,
   "end": 146.87
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay.",
   "start": 147.75,
   "end": 148.19
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "So, two things. First, your hypothyroidism from Hashimoto's. The TSH was a little high and I think part of that is the way you're taking the pill. coffee and calcium both block absorption, take the levathuric sign alone with water first thing in the morning, at least 30 to 60 minutes before coffee or breakfast, and take the calcium at least four hours later with dinner is easiest.",
   "start": 148.73,
   "end": 171.85
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Oh, I had no idea.",
   "start": 172.55,
   "end": 173.91
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Keep the dose at 88 micrograms for now. I'll recheck the TSH and a free T4 in six weeks once you've been taking it the right way. Stop the biotin gummy three days before that blood draw because biotin can throw off thyroid tests.",
   "start": 174.59,
   "end": 190.83
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, and if it's still high?",
   "start": 191.73,
   "end": 193.01
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "If the TSH is still above 4 .5, we'd go up to 100 micrograms, but let's see first. Second, your cholesterol is high and an underactive thyroid can raise cholesterol, so I'd like a fasting lipid panel with the thyroid labs and then we'll talk about your overall heart risk, especially with your father's history. Meanwhile, more fiber, less saturated fat, and regular exercise.",
   "start": 193.77,
   "end": 220.17
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "That sounds reasonable.",
   "start": 220.85,
   "end": 221.95
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'll see you in six to eight weeks after the labs. Can I get an email for the portal?",
   "start": 222.69,
   "end": 227.61
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Sure, it's spetrova79 at example .com.",
   "start": 228.63,
   "end": 232.01
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Perfect. Welcome to the practice, Svetlana.",
   "start": 233.15,
   "end": 235.47
  }
 ],
